# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Snap Glow — environment variables
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values only when you
# connect a domain or backend. The shipped site runs WITHOUT any of these:
# everything is stored locally in the browser.
#
#   Windows PowerShell:  Copy-Item .env.example .env
#   macOS / Linux:       cp .env.example .env
#
# NEVER put real secrets in this file or commit a filled-in `.env`.

# Public site URL used for canonical links, sitemap and share URLs.
# Use your real production domain here, e.g. https://www.snapglow.example
VITE_SITE_URL=https://www.your-domain.com

# ── Supabase upgrade path (optional — see docs/BACKEND_SETUP.md) ──
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://xyzcompany.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key-here
#
# IMPORTANT: the anon key is public by design, but the SERVICE ROLE key
# must NEVER appear in frontend code or in this file. Keep it server-side.
